{"card_hash": "dadcf337a45e919db5545624e00469ee0660b2277b5f524638b463566fe379a2", "channel": "Edje Electronics", "chars": 18942, "chars_all_clips": 18942, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 19, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=r0RspiLG260\u0026t=13s", "end": 77.48, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "7c37a600544c581ecb82437acc3ae78e3a28963681622faa49490f616a796c8c", "start": 13.6, "text": "Hey everyone, today we're going to walk through\\h training a YOLO model inside Google Colab. I'll\\h\\h go through the process of gathering a data set\\h training the model in Colab and then running it\\h\\h locally on your PC with a custom Pyth", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=r0RspiLG260\u0026t=243s", "end": 334.4, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "bdd70e24c8ebeb9d7070e8f98b5b0e00518d2edcf789f220fc618c8979e6b7f2", "start": 243.84, "text": "Once it's installed start Label Studio\\h by issuing \"label-studio start\". After a few seconds, Label Studio will start in\\h a new web browser window. Label Studio runs on\\h\\h a server that's hosted locally on your computer,\\h and you intera", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=r0RspiLG260\u0026t=466s", "end": 553.44, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "86577a68dcdef26743ac073197b16a59c2931e752b0c9f4c511f83a5ab2b9320", "start": 466.16, "text": "Once you've labeled all your images,\\h it's time to export them. Click the\\h\\h project name at the top of the window and\\h then click the Export button. Scroll down\\h\\h and select the YOLO export option and then\\h click Export. Label Studio", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=r0RspiLG260\u0026t=715s", "end": 804.36, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "4f5b4678278032c2df8c74c23aa7bbf1042489f7f4bd284e707cd8b820b8a66f", "start": 715.84, "text": "Okay, we're finally ready to run training! But\\h there's a few important parameters we need to\\h\\h decide on first. We need to pick which YOLO\\h model we want to use. There's a variety of\\h\\h YOLO architectures and model sizes. YOLO11 is th", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=r0RspiLG260\u0026t=872s", "end": 986.12, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "9b3beb0295750490edecd141b38c40c3157fe01712fa5e77581924fa461805c2", "start": 872.88, "text": "When training finishes, the best\\h model weights will be saved in\\h\\h runs/detect/train/weights/best.pt. The results.png\\h file shows how metrics like loss, precision,\\h\\h recall, and mAP progressed over each training\\h epoch. Let's make th", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=r0RspiLG260\u0026t=1215s", "end": 1285.598, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "36a8a2d1e09d7e6c519188916d85517637059cdc02b8dd5aa2e1a43dcf1a6ff9", "start": 1215.56, "text": "Again, a window will appear\\h showing detection results. To see a full description of how to use\\h yolo_detect.py, see the readme file in\\h\\h the Train-YOLO-Models GitHub repository\\h linked in the video description below. Okay, congratulat", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "Social Media Research", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=r0RspiLG260\u0026t=13s", "end": 77.48, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "7c37a600544c581ecb82437acc3ae78e3a28963681622faa49490f616a796c8c", "start": 13.6, "text": "Hey everyone, today we're going to walk through\\h training a YOLO model inside Google Colab. I'll\\h\\h go through the process of gathering a data set\\h training the model in Colab and then running it\\h\\h locally on your PC with a custom Pyth", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=r0RspiLG260\u0026t=243s", "end": 334.4, "ev